infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Branched vs branchless: predictability decides
  desc Same conditional — a normal if/else wins when the branch is predictable, branchless wins when it is random
  compares
    - label Branched if/else — runs one path
      children
        - label Predictable 95%+: ~0 extra cycles
          desc Predictor guesses right, so only the taken path executes and the branch is essentially free
        - label Unpredictable 50/50: 15-30 cycles per miss
          desc Half the iterations mispredict and flush the pipeline — the worst case for the predictor
        - label Best when the branch is predictable
          desc Sorted or regular data: skipping the other path's compute beats always doing both
    - label Branchless / CMOV — runs both paths
      children
        - label No branch, no misprediction ever
          desc A conditional move or arithmetic select removes the pipeline flush entirely
        - label Unpredictable 50/50: 2-5x faster
          desc Eliminating the flush outweighs always computing both sides of the conditional
        - label Best when the miss rate is high
          desc Random data you cannot sort; confirm with perf stat branch-misses above ~5%
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6
